# Arch Linux Bare Metal: The ThinkPad Pilot

This repository documents my journey of installing and configuring Arch Linux on bare metal. 

> **Current Status:** **Testing Phase**. 
> I am currently running this setup on a secondary **ThinkPad** to refine my workflow, 
test hardware compatibility, and script my configuration before migrating to my primary daily driver.

---

## Hardware Specs (The Pilot Rig)
* **Model:** Lenovo ThinkPad T480
* **CPU:** Intel Core i5-5300
* **RAM:** 8 GB
* **Storage:** 300 GB HDD
* **Goal:** Achieve a stable, bloat-free environment that 
will prepare me for a switch to arch full time on my daily laptop 

---

## System Architecture & Partitioning
The system uses **UEFI/GPT** for modern compatibility.

| Partition | Mount Point | Type | Size | Notes |

| `/dev/sda1` | `/boot` | FAT32 | 512 M | Larger for multiple kernels |
| `/dev/sda2` | `[SWAP]` | Swap | 8 GB | For Hibernation/RAM overflow |
| `/dev/sda3` | `/` | Linux Filesystem | Remainder | All storage for root directory |

